967 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Diagram of concentric circles representing a rights-respecting, needs-providing socio-ecosystem. At the center is the child as the holder of human rights. Surrounding layers include Microsystem \(families, communities\), Mesosystem \(linkages between systems\), Exosystem \(parents and community\), Macrosystem \(social and cultural norms\), Chronosystem \(commitment over time\), and Geo-Political system \(upholding laws like UNCRC\).) /K 997 0 R /P 240 0 R /Pg 230 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
968 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Concentric circle diagram titled "Socio-ecosophere in Gaza \(August 2025\)" illustrating various systems. The outermost circle, "Geo-Political system," indicates discarded international laws and lack of protection for children. "Chronosystem" highlights historical conflict and trauma. "Macrosystem" shows destroyed infrastructure and absent policy. "Exosystem" represents decimated social supports. "Mesosystem" refers to fractured systems by destruction scale. "Microsystem" features families and essential services under attack, culminating in "Egregious violations of children's rights.") /K 998 0 R /P 240 0 R /Pg 233 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
969 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Diagram comparing the socio-ecosphere in Gaza before October 2023 and in August 2025. The left side shows existing rights violations with less severe conditions, while the right side illustrates escalating violations, including the destruction of infrastructure and extensive harm to children. The bottom table presents data on rights violations, survival, health, education, and healthcare, showing a stark worsening of conditions by August 2025, including significant increases in child mortality and school and hospital damages.) /K 999 0 R /P 240 0 R /Pg 234 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
